  "ai_language_tip": "Speak clear, polite standard Macedonian (mk, Cyrillic); Albanian (sq) is widely used in Skopje's western areas, Tetovo, Gostivar and Struga, so switch if the owner answers in it; Serbian is understood by older people; English works with younger staff and in Ohrid tourism.",
  "english_ok": "sometimes — Good among younger urban staff and in Ohrid; limited at public clinics and offices.",
  "politeness": "Formal 'Вие', 'господине/госпоѓо'; open with 'Добар ден' and say for whom you call; close with 'Благодарам, довидување'.",
  "name_tip": "Surname first in bookings; Macedonian surnames change by gender (-ски / -ска, e.g. Петровски / Петровска); spell foreign names letter by letter and expect Cyrillic writing.",
  "phone_tip": "Mobile 07x xxx xxx (9 digits with 0), Skopje landline 02 + 7 digits, +389; Viber on the same number is common.",
  "time_tip": "'седум и пол' = 7:30 and 'осум без петнаесет' = 7:45 (no half-before trap in standard usage); read back in 24h.",
  "number_tip": "People counted with special forms ('двајца', 'тројца'); prices in denars (MKD), sometimes quoted in euro; read phones in groups.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid lunch 13:00–15:00, dinner peak 20:00–22:00, calls after 21:00 and Sundays for offices; public clinics answer best early morning.",
  "closed_days": "Shops open on Sundays (with shorter hours); holidays include 1 January, Orthodox Christmas 7 January, Orthodox Easter Monday, 1 May, 24 May, 2 August, 8 September, Eid al-Fitr, 11 and 23 October, 8 December.",
  "booking_channels": "Moj termin (national e-health system) for public specialist appointments through the GP; phone, Viber and Instagram for restaurants, salons and garages; Wolt and local apps (e.g. Korpa) for delivery.",
  "voice_menu": "Operators (A1, Makedonski Telekom), banks and Pošta use IVR; small venues answer directly.",
  "callback_habits": "Viber and phone call-backs are the norm; Moj termin issues electronic referrals and appointment slips; private clinics may SMS.",
